  "provider_query": "MDN page for the Request.redirect property",
  "answer": "**Primary page:** [Request: redirect property – MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/redirect)\n\n- **`Request.redirect`** is a read-only property of the Fetch API `Request` interface. It holds the mode for how redirects are handled. Available in Web Workers; widely available since March 2017. [[1]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/redirect)\n- **Value:** a `RequestRedirect` enum string: `follow`, `error`, or `manual`. Default if omitted at construction: `follow`. [[1]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/redirect)\n- **Example:**\n  ```js\n  const myRequest = new Request(\"flowers.jpg\");\n  const myCred = myRequest.redirect;\n  ```\n  [[1]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/redirect)\n- Spec: Fetch standard (`dom-request-redirect`). Last modified on MDN: 20 Sep 2026. [[1]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/redirect)\n\n**Related MDN pages**\n\n1. [Request – Web APIs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request) — lists `Request.redirect` among instance properties (`follow` | `error` | `manual`). [[2]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request)\n2. [Request() constructor](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/Request) — creates a `Request`; redirect mode is set via options when the request is created. [[3]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/Request)\n3. [Redirections in HTTP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/Redirections) — HTTP 3xx redirects and `Location` behavior (server-side context for the client redirect mode). [[4]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/Redirections)\n4. [Location header](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Location) — header used with redirect responses. [[5]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Location)\n5. [308 Permanent Redirect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status/308) — permanent redirect status that preserves method and body. [[6]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Status/308)\n\n**Not the same API**\n\n- [declarativeNetRequest.Redirect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/declarativeNetRequest/Redirect) — extension rule redirect config, not `Request.redirect`. [[7]](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/declarativeNetRequest/Redirect)",
